{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013T5TzHi9Wwfmm3qwMEmJwG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: add-protocol-decoder\n3\tdescription: Use when adding a new device protocol or changing how an existing protocol decodes messages or encodes commands.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Add or change a protocol decoder\n7\t\n8\tBackground: [docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md](../../../docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md).\n9\t\n10\t1. Get a real sample message from the task or issue (hex for binary, text otherwise). Do not invent sample data: if there is none, stop and ask.\n11\t2. Look for an existing protocol with the same format first: `grep -ril \"<vendor or keyword>\" src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol`. Many devices reuse GT06, H02, Teltonika, Meitrack or similar formats; extending a decoder is better than adding a protocol.\n12\t3. To change an existing protocol, add the sample to `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` first, for example:\n13\t   ```java\n14\t   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));   // no position expected\n15\t   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"7979...0d0a\"),\n16\t           position(Checks.ATTRIBUTES).attribute(Position.KEY_POWER, 4.05));\n17\t   ```\n18\t   The number of `position(...)` arguments is the number of positions expected. `position()` (= `Checks.ALL`) checks that time, coordinates, speed and course are in valid ranges; `Checks.ATTRIBUTES` checks the attributes only; `Checks.NONE` checks only what you chain (`.attribute(...)`). See `src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java`.\n19\t   Run it and see it fail: `make test TESTS=org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest`.\n20\t4. For a new protocol, create in `src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/`, copying a similar protocol:\n21\t   - `<Name>Protocol.java` extends `BaseProtocol`; adds a `TrackerServer` (second argument `true` for UDP) and its handlers in `addProtocolHandlers`.\n22\t   - `<Name>FrameDecoder.java` if the transport is a stream with no simple delimiter (otherwise use `CharacterDelimiterFrameDecoder` or `LineBasedFrameDecoder` in the pipeline).\n23\t   - `<Name>ProtocolDecoder.java` extends `BaseProtocolDecoder`; use `getDeviceSession(...)`, `Parser`/`PatternBuilder` for text, `ByteBuf` and `BitUtil` for binary.\n24\t   - `<Name>ProtocolEncoder.java` only if the device accepts commands, and list them with `setSupportedDataCommands`.\n25\t5. Register a new protocol in `src/main/java/org/traccar/config/ProtocolConfig.java`: add the import and `put(<Name>Protocol.class, <port>);` with the next free port after the last entry.\n26\t6. Create `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` (extends `ProtocolTest`, `var decoder = inject(new <Name>ProtocolDecoder(null));`) and, if there is a frame decoder, `<Name>FrameDecoderTest.java`.\n27\t7. Use the standard keys in `src/main/java/org/traccar/model/Position.java` (`KEY_*`, `ALARM_*`) before inventing attribute names.\n28\t8. Run `make check-fast`. Checkstyle often flags line length and import order in decoders.\n29\t9. Optional end-to-end check: `make dev`, then send the sample with `tools/hex.sh <port> <hex>` and look for the decoded position in the console log.\n30\t10. Commit as `Decode <vendor> <message type>` or `Add <Name> protocol`, following `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf8f1475-228d-4796-ae58-ad0f616495b9","uuid":"f9e152db-3b2e-4ea4-b617-df4025f7f9ef","timestamp":"2026-11-02T06:43:37.621Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/traccar/bench/trees/traccar-2-harness-haiku/.agents/skills/add-protocol-decoder/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: add-protocol-decoder\ndescription: Use when adding a new device protocol or changing how an existing protocol decodes messages or encodes commands.\n---\n\n# Add or change a protocol decoder\n\nBackground: [docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md](../../../docs/decisions/0002-one-netty-decoder-per-protocol.md).\n\n1. Get a real sample message from the task or issue (hex for binary, text otherwise). Do not invent sample data: if there is none, stop and ask.\n2. Look for an existing protocol with the same format first: `grep -ril \"<vendor or keyword>\" src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol`. Many devices reuse GT06, H02, Teltonika, Meitrack or similar formats; extending a decoder is better than adding a protocol.\n3. To change an existing protocol, add the sample to `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` first, for example:\n   ```java\n   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"78780D01086471700328358100093F040D0A\"));   // no position expected\n   verifyDecode(decoder, binary(\"7979...0d0a\"),\n           position(Checks.ATTRIBUTES).attribute(Position.KEY_POWER, 4.05));\n   ```\n   The number of `position(...)` arguments is the number of positions expected. `position()` (= `Checks.ALL`) checks that time, coordinates, speed and course are in valid ranges; `Checks.ATTRIBUTES` checks the attributes only; `Checks.NONE` checks only what you chain (`.attribute(...)`). See `src/test/java/org/traccar/ProtocolTest.java`.\n   Run it and see it fail: `make test TESTS=org.traccar.protocol.Gt06ProtocolDecoderTest`.\n4. For a new protocol, create in `src/main/java/org/traccar/protocol/`, copying a similar protocol:\n   - `<Name>Protocol.java` extends `BaseProtocol`; adds a `TrackerServer` (second argument `true` for UDP) and its handlers in `addProtocolHandlers`.\n   - `<Name>FrameDecoder.java` if the transport is a stream with no simple delimiter (otherwise use `CharacterDelimiterFrameDecoder` or `LineBasedFrameDecoder` in the pipeline).\n   - `<Name>ProtocolDecoder.java` extends `BaseProtocolDecoder`; use `getDeviceSession(...)`, `Parser`/`PatternBuilder` for text, `ByteBuf` and `BitUtil` for binary.\n   - `<Name>ProtocolEncoder.java` only if the device accepts commands, and list them with `setSupportedDataCommands`.\n5. Register a new protocol in `src/main/java/org/traccar/config/ProtocolConfig.java`: add the import and `put(<Name>Protocol.class, <port>);` with the next free port after the last entry.\n6. Create `src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol/<Name>ProtocolDecoderTest.java` (extends `ProtocolTest`, `var decoder = inject(new <Name>ProtocolDecoder(null));`) and, if there is a frame decoder, `<Name>FrameDecoderTest.java`.\n7. Use the standard keys in `src/main/java/org/traccar/model/Position.java` (`KEY_*`, `ALARM_*`) before inventing attribute names.\n8. Run `make check-fast`. Checkstyle often flags line length and import order in decoders.\n9. Optional end-to-end check: `make dev`, then send the sample with `tools/hex.sh <port> <hex>` and look for the decoded position in the console log.\n10. Commit as `Decode <vendor> <message type>` or `Add <Name> protocol`, following `CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013T5TzHi9Wwfmm3qwMEmJwG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
